UID:movie-1776026@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261102T142919Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Borrowed from the Earth
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Zach Johaneson\n\nTells the story of the powerful
  connection between the Blackfeet people and horses\, and how that life-
 giving relationship remains alive today. Throughout their histories\, bo
 th horse and Indigenous people have been corralled - horses by fences\, 
 and Indigenous people onto reservations. Yet centuries-long attempts to 
 subdue both ultimately strengthened the bond between them. Saddle up for
  a visually poetic journey from the origin story of the horse to the mod
 ern day Indian Relay Race. Filmed on the Blackfeet Reservation in Browni
 ng\, Montana.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1776026
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1776026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
