UID:movie-1645388@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261102T142919Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:The Last of the Lookouts
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Ryan Wilkes\n\nHigh atop Sinkut Mountain in north
 ern British Columbia\, Bart Vanderlinde begins each summer's day the way
  he has for the past nine years: scanning the forest for smoke. He's amo
 ng the last lookout people in the province. Where three hundred lookouts
  once formed an interconnected network across the region\, Bart now ofte
 n keeps watch alone. This is an intimate portrait of a man and a profess
 ion facing obsolescence. The film gives insight into the craft of fire d
 etection while capturing the quiet solitude of a life lived in observati
 on.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1645388
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1645388
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1807886@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261102T142919Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Building Apollo 13
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Bianca Fidani\n\nWhat begins as a challenge on th
 e rock becomes a profound process of dedication and commitment. Caro Nor
 th\, Fay Manners\, Rocio Rodriguez Guiñazú and Belén Prados devote th
 eir time\, bodies\, and hearts to opening a new route in a remote place\
 , Turbio IV in Patagonia\, Argentina\, building not only a challenge but
  also a way of inhabiting and sharing the mountain. What makes it unique
  is their willingness to dedicate the necessary time and care to leave t
 he route immaculate and safe for other climbers to enjoy; not simply to 
 climb a wall\, but to create something that can be shared with others.\n
 \nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1807886
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1807886
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
