SUMMARY:Against the Clock
DESCRIPTION:Directed by John Baikie\n\nA short documentary exploring the 
 life and passion of cyclist Alasdair Washington. Blending race footage w
 ith moments of personal reflection\, the film offers an honest portrait 
 of his lasting connection to the sport. It looks at the discipline\, det
 ermination and enjoyment that continue to fuel his competitive spirit. R
 ather than focusing on results alone\, the story captures the essence of
  what it means to keep showing up and pushing forward. What keeps the wh
 eels turning when time refuses to slow down? Both intimate and authentic
 \, the film celebrates a lifelong passion for cycling and community.\n\n
 https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1797220
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1797220
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1808194@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261102T142919Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Elsewhere: Randi Skaug
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Toby Roney\n\nRandi Skaug was the first Norwegian
  woman to climb Mount Everest and went on to complete the Seven Summits.
  She has led expeditions around the world\, written books and inspired t
 housands of people to embrace the outdoors. Now going through cancer tre
 atment and unable to return to her remote island house\, Randi welcomes 
 us into her eclectic home in Oslo. As her world grows smaller\, her pers
 pective grows clearer. For Randi\, a lifetime of extraordinary achieveme
 nt has led to one simple conclusion: be kind.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.
 org/movie/1808194
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1808194
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1807273@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261102T142919Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Beura
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Gregor D. Sinclair\n\nThe tale of the Cailleach B
 heur\, the Celtic goddess of nature\, storms and winter\, is well known 
 to many in the Gàidhealtachd. Said to have carved the mountains and gle
 ns with ice\, and borne the islands like children on her back\, the Cail
 leach disappeared long ago leaving us only with her song – a sad\, cau
 tionary tale. This Gaelic arts project brings music\, film and verse tog
 ether to reimagine Cailleach’s story for the modern era.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.themoviedb.org/movie/1807273
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1807273
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
