SUMMARY:All Rivers Spill Their Stories to the Sea
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Jeanie Finlay\n\nOn England’s North East coast\
 , where rivers\, heavy industry and the sea have shaped lives for genera
 tions\, fisherman Stan Rennie is watching the world he knows disappear. 
 His family have worked these waters for generations. Then\, almost overn
 ight\, thousands of dead crabs and lobsters wash ashore\, and a communit
 y already living with uncertainty is pushed into crisis. Teesside filmma
 ker Jeanie Finlay brings warmth\, wit and deep local feeling to this Dav
 id-and-Goliath story of environmental damage\, official evasions and wor
 king-class resilience. At its centre is Stan: funny\, stubborn\, vulnera
 ble and increasingly determined to be heard.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.o
 rg/movie/1620941
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1620941
